{"text": "We often hear: you're offering a template. The alternative is a unique design. But nothing is entirely unique, and a design starts to age from day one. In the mock-up, made-up content looks great. Real content is added by the school itself. One colleague prepared a text, another pasted it as it came. The head got an email and asked to change the menu. Parents missed a document, so it was moved “higher”. Nobody means any harm. The website simply becomes everyone's, and no one's. That's how the twelve mistakes that catch the eye the most are born. Each mistake looks like a detail. Together, they make a good school look worse than it is. Now multiply it by a hundred schools. Five hundred… and more. Schools learn from each other. Sadly, mistakes travel that way too. The same mistakes, thousands of times. That's how the whole system looks.\n\nThank you for watching.", "alignment": {"characters": ["W", "e", " ", "o", "f", "t", "e", "n", " ", "h", "e", "a", "r", ":", " ", "y", "o", "u", "'", "r", "e", " ", "o", "f", "f", "e", "r", "i", "n", "g", " ", "a", " ", "t", "e", "m", "p", "l", "a", "t", "e", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "a", "l", "t", "e", "r", "n", "a", "t", "i", "v", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "a", " ", "u", "n", "i", "q", "u", "e", " ", "d", "e", "s", "i", "g", "n", ".", " ", "B", "u", "t", " ", "n", "o", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", " ", "i", "s", " ", "e", "n", "t", "i", "r", "e", "l", "y", " ", "u", "n", "i", "q", "u", "e", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "a", " ", "d", "e", "s", "i", "g", "n", " ", "s", "t", "a", "r", "t", "s", " ", "t", "o", " ", "a", "g", "e", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "d", "a", "y", " ", "o", "n", "e", ".", " ", "I", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "o", "c", "k", "-", "u", "p", ",", " ", "m", "a", "d", "e", "-", "u", "p", " ", "c", "o", "n", "t", "e", "n", "t", " ", "l", "o", "o", "k", "s", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", ".", " ", "R", "e", "a", "l", " ", "c", "o", "n", "t", "e", "n", "t", " ", "i", "s", " ", "a", "d", "d", "e", 